    "result": "Excellent! The fix is working correctly. Both files are now created:\n\n1. \u2705 `FRAI-SPEC.md` \n2. \u2705 `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`\n\n**Summary of the fix:**\n\nThe bug was in how the `frai` CLI passes arguments to the `frai-gate` subcommand. Commander.js was consuming the `--ci` flag at the main program level rather than passing it through to the gate command.\n\n**The solution:** Instead of relying on commander.js's parsed arguments, I modified the gate command handler to extract all remaining arguments directly from `process.argv`, which preserves flags and options that would otherwise be consumed by the argument parser. This way, everything after the `gate` keyword is passed through untouched to the frai-gate CLI, which handles its own parsing.\n\nThe fix allows `frai gate init --ci` to work identically to running `frai-gate init --ci` directly.",
